    "category": "games",
    "title": "The Round That Did Not Count",
    "passage": "Max and Priya made a game in which players rolled a ball towards three boxes. The nearest box was worth one point, and the farthest was worth three. Priya scored eight points before Max noticed that one box had moved. Each time the ball touched it, the light box slid a little farther across the floor. Max had been playing after Priya, so his throws had started with the box farther away. They put a book inside each box to stop it moving. Priya suggested starting again with no points. Max agreed, and they tested one throw each before the new round. This time, all three boxes stayed in place. Priya still scored eight points. Max smiled and said he could believe those eight much more easily.",
